      "message": "I intentionally kept that, even though it\u0027s UNUSED_ATTR, as I think the addr/transport tuple should be the *only* way to determine a link.\n\n(I still am on a mission to combine addr/addr_with_type as I think they both serve the same purpose and should be related somehow.  Then the find_connected_Device would be addr_of_some_kind, transport, and if the transport is classic, addr_of_some_kind is Address, and le, it\u0027s addr_with_type.)\n\nUnf. the transport wasn\u0027t considered in the architecture, and I wanted it preserved to future generations would consider this transport as an essential part of determining a link state.\n\nIt\u0027s the bta layer which itself is a `shim` layer, and eventually would be re-absorbed back into the stack layer, or promoted into it\u0027s own module, or simply removed as there is a lot of duplicated state here.",
